Hello,

In regards to the withdrawal of service, once processed,  the Branch will i=
nvite the tenants affected by the withdrawal to come to the Branch, during =
office hours, to inspect the landlord=E2=80=99s application and supporting =
material.

Please see  link for more information about a withdrawal of service.

Residential Tenancies Branch | Province of Manitoba (gov.mb.ca)<https://www=
.gov.mb.ca/cca/rtb/ot/gbook/s13rentreg_withdrawal-reducofservice14.html>
If you suffered a financial loss because of the landlord, you have the righ=
t to file a claim against the landlord. You may file a claim by filling out=
 the tenant claim form with a $50.00 filing fee and submit it back to the b=
ranch and a hearing will be scheduled where there hearing officer will issu=
e an order with the decision.

Thank you,
CMP/RTB

